<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Detroit</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Detroit is a city in Michigan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, on the Detroit River between Lake Erie and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-huron">Lake Huron</a>. It was founded in 1701 by Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac as Fort Pontchartrain du Détroit, a French fur-trading post, and passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1760. The British kept it until 1796, and in August 1812 British and Native forces captured it from the Americans. In the 20th century it became the centre of the US car industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/detroit.jpg" alt="Detroit" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TheWxResearcher · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detroit_Skyline_from_Windsor_2025-09-01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
